743
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,100
when you get here.

744
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:48,700
- I think maybe one plane
landing at a time, please.

745
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:50,633
(upbeat instrumental jazz)

746
00:26:50,633 --> 00:26:53,733
- [Servo] That's
sexy land. (growls)

747
00:26:53,733 --> 00:26:58,067
- [Mike] Hey move over a
little, scooch, scooch over.

748
00:26:58,067 --> 00:27:01,533
- [Servo] The exotic Zeppelins
of Led down the Mississippi.

749
00:27:01,533 --> 00:27:06,533
The year is 1952, a very
young Stan Getz at the mic.

750
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:10,000
The Jackie Gleason show!

751
00:27:13,167 --> 00:27:14,467
- [Mike] We bring
you into the hangar

752
00:27:14,467 --> 00:27:16,767
in a relaxed kind of way.

753
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:21,000
- [Servo] Tell the tower
the music's a little loud.

754
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,433
- The military
has so much money,

755
00:27:22,433 --> 00:27:25,600
they actually have Nelson
Riddle in the tower.

756
00:27:27,200 --> 00:27:31,167
♪ Please be careful
of the intake. ♪

757
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:34,567
- [Mike] I've had to
go potty since Toma.

758
00:27:34,567 --> 00:27:37,300
- Could be better,
failed to yield.

759
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:40,400
- [Mike] F minus.

760
00:27:41,300 --> 00:27:42,133
- [Servo] Oh no.

761
00:27:44,700 --> 00:27:46,933
- Hey, James Carville.

762
00:27:46,933 --> 00:27:49,600
(powering down)

763
00:27:50,767 --> 00:27:52,100
- I see you've been
upping the newcomers.

764
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:53,533
What do they think
of the Starfighters?

765
00:27:53,533 --> 00:27:54,900
- Well, I don't know about York,

766
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:56,533
but Witkowski seems to
have been born in one.

767
00:27:56,533 --> 00:27:58,000
- [Mike] Ooh.

768
00:27:58,000 --> 00:27:59,000
- Oh yeah, with the way
his old man feels about it?

769
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,533
Why what happened?

770
00:28:00,533 --> 00:28:02,000
- Well, after a half an
hour of some familiarization

771
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,500
flying, I gave him
the feel of it.

772
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:04,933
He made me ashamed
of the thousand hours

773
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:06,067
I've logged in this bird.

774
00:28:06,067 --> 00:28:07,500
- What's the beef, Bob?

775
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:08,700
- Well, nothing
Colonel, but frankly,

776
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:10,467
I never saw a neophyte
handle an airplane

777
00:28:10,467 --> 00:28:11,767
the way Witkowski did.

778
00:28:11,767 --> 00:28:13,000
- [Mike] What's a neophyte, Bob?

779
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:14,500
- Sure, he was a little
sloppy on the controls

780
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:16,033
at the start, but after he got
used to the characteristics,

781
00:28:16,033 --> 00:28:18,200
he threw the book at it, doing
his best to annihilate space.

782
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,033
- You mean he was showing off?

783
00:28:19,033 --> 00:28:20,767
- Not at all.

784
00:28:20,767 --> 00:28:23,167
No, Witkowski's the start of
a darn good fighter pilot.

785
00:28:23,167 --> 00:28:24,367
- [Servo] Why don't
you marry him?

786
00:28:24,367 --> 00:28:25,600
- He was obviously
trained right.

787
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:26,800
But more than that,
there's something

788
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:27,933
bringing this drive out in him.

789
00:28:27,933 --> 00:28:28,867
- Of course.

790
00:28:28,867 --> 00:28:30,100
- The congressman?

791
00:28:30,100 --> 00:28:31,200
- Oh maybe, but do you
know flying a plane

792
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:32,200
is like making love?

793
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,433
- [Mike] Uh, you have to pay?

794
00:28:33,433 --> 00:28:34,600
- Once you've had a
little experience,

795
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:37,400
every operator thinks
he's an expert.

796
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:39,267
♪ The marriage to build a sky. ♪

797
00:28:39,267 --> 00:28:41,567
- [Mike] Tell me
more about love.

798
00:28:41,567 --> 00:28:43,600
- [Servo] Where is
the stupid ladder guy?

799
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:48,233
- Hey, there's
airplanes around here.

800
00:28:49,833 --> 00:28:51,633
- [Mike] Up, up, and away.

801
00:28:51,633 --> 00:28:53,667
- Well, hello there.

802
00:28:53,667 --> 00:28:55,900
- Well, hello there, yourself.

803
00:28:55,900 --> 00:28:57,067
- She's bing-a-ling.

804
00:28:57,067 --> 00:28:58,833
- Picture of contentment
while we hesitated

805
00:28:58,833 --> 00:28:59,833
about interrupting.

806
00:28:59,833 --> 00:29:01,133
- Not at all.

807
00:29:01,133 --> 00:29:02,700
Say fellas, this
is my wife, Betty.

808
00:29:02,700 --> 00:29:05,567
Betty, this is John
Witkowski and Bill York.

809
00:29:05,567 --> 00:29:07,100
- [Servo] We call 'em
Pinkidink and Porkboy.

810
00:29:07,100 --> 00:29:09,033
- Come on, have a seat, you
guys aren't going anywhere.

811
00:29:09,033 --> 00:29:10,567
- Sure will.

812
00:29:10,567 --> 00:29:11,500
- [Mike] You don't mind if
we continue to make love.

813
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:12,733
- Some friends at the club.

814
00:29:12,733 --> 00:29:14,267
- Gene told me he
was starting off

815
00:29:14,267 --> 00:29:15,533
with a couple bachelors.

816
00:29:15,533 --> 00:29:17,367
- Oh, footloose and fancy-free,

817
00:29:17,367 --> 00:29:18,733
and we're on the prowl.

818
00:29:18,733 --> 00:29:19,667
(growls)

819
00:29:19,667 --> 00:29:20,900
- Well, we can't really say.

820
00:29:20,900 --> 00:29:23,300
We really haven't
started to look.

821
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:24,667
What are you doing tonight?

822
00:29:24,667 --> 00:29:27,167
- Ha, hey, you really
are on the prowl.

823
00:29:27,167 --> 00:29:28,367
- You stay out of this.

824
00:29:28,367 --> 00:29:29,633
- Yes, stay out of this.

825
00:29:29,633 --> 00:29:30,867
- [Servo] Honey.

826
00:29:30,867 --> 00:29:31,667
- Now, which one of
you two nice young men

827
00:29:31,667 --> 00:29:32,433
is looking for a date?

828
00:29:32,433 --> 00:29:33,267
- Me.

829
00:29:33,267 --> 00:29:34,433
- Right here.

830
00:29:34,433 --> 00:29:35,700
- Well, not to
change the subject,

831
00:29:35,700 --> 00:29:38,133
but just how did it go
out there today, huh?

832
00:29:38,133 --> 00:29:39,867
- Gene, you'll never believe it.

833
00:29:39,867 --> 00:29:41,800
I don't know how to explain
it, you'll never believe it.

834
00:29:41,800 --> 00:29:43,933
That bird really wants to go.

835
00:29:43,933 --> 00:29:45,433
- [Mike] I don't believe it.

836
00:29:45,433 --> 00:29:46,700
- It was even more than
Colonel Hunt said it was.

837
00:29:46,700 --> 00:29:49,067
You know, I actually
thought that it was

838
00:29:49,067 --> 00:29:51,033
gonna get away from under
us while we were taking off.

839
00:29:51,033 --> 00:29:52,100
- [Mike] Yeah, great.

840
00:29:52,100 --> 00:29:53,367
Can we order?

841
00:29:53,367 --> 00:29:54,800
- I've never experienced
anything like it before.

842
00:29:54,800 --> 00:29:56,000
Never before.

843
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,100
Remember when we were
making the change?

844
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:57,967
- [Mike] Oh boy.

845
00:29:57,967 --> 00:29:59,433
- Yeah.

846
00:29:59,433 --> 00:30:02,800
- Believe me, this change
is even more terrific.

847
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:04,800
- Uh, you mean, you're
really sold on it, huh?

848
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:05,800
- Oh!

849
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:06,733
- [Mike] No.

850
00:30:06,733 --> 00:30:07,900
- I signed the contract today.

851
00:30:07,900 --> 00:30:09,000
- [Servo] He's a
regular Sam Levenson.

852
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:10,433
- Did you hear what he says?

853
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:11,700
I mean, about the wonderful
flight you had today?

854
00:30:11,700 --> 00:30:13,733
- Everything he says and
an awful lot more too.

855
00:30:13,733 --> 00:30:15,200
(munching sounds)

856
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,300
Gene leaves off on his
first ride in the morning.

857
00:30:16,300 --> 00:30:17,500
- Yeah, and I can hardly wait.

858
00:30:17,500 --> 00:30:19,567
Say, say look, why
don't you guys join us

859
00:30:19,567 --> 00:30:20,867
for dinner tonight, come on.

860
00:30:20,867 --> 00:30:22,033
- Aw, negative, but thanks.

861
00:30:22,033 --> 00:30:23,333
I had a snack a
little while earlier.

862
00:30:23,333 --> 00:30:24,600
Right now, all I want to do is

863
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:26,200
make friends with the bartender.

864
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:27,433
- [Servo] (laughs) Drink
'till I wet myself.

865
00:30:27,433 --> 00:30:28,867
- Gene, I think I'll
pass on that too.

866
00:30:28,867 --> 00:30:30,100
You get me a day, and I'll

867
00:30:30,100 --> 00:30:33,567
take you up on that
dinner offering, okay?

868
00:30:33,567 --> 00:30:35,167
- We'll see you, nice
meeting you, Betty.

869
00:30:35,167 --> 00:30:36,733
- [Mike] It was a
great, great scene.

870
00:30:36,733 --> 00:30:38,033
- You know, John, I
never really realized

871
00:30:38,033 --> 00:30:39,333
what a tiger you are.

872
00:30:39,333 --> 00:30:40,767
- Sh, not here.

873
00:30:40,767 --> 00:30:43,233
- Why I'm just as
sociable as the next guy.

874
00:30:43,233 --> 00:30:45,167
- Oh, I mean about
on that flight today.

875
00:30:45,167 --> 00:30:46,767
Boy, you were really
rocking it around.

876
00:30:46,767 --> 00:30:47,733
- What do you mean?

877
00:30:47,733 --> 00:30:49,267
Stevens gave me the controls

878
00:30:49,267 --> 00:30:50,467
and told me not to break
the airplane, that's all.

879
00:30:50,467 --> 00:30:51,300
- Yeah, I know.

880
00:30:51,300 --> 00:30:52,600
- [Servo] Don't pout.

881
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,567
- You've been holding
out on me, old buddy.

882
00:30:53,567 --> 00:30:54,767
- Oh, it's not the first time

883
00:30:54,767 --> 00:30:56,100
either of us have been in a jet.

884
00:30:56,100 --> 00:30:58,200
- First time on one of
these babies for me.

885
00:30:58,200 --> 00:31:00,167
- [Mike] Oh, that Vodka, mm.

886
00:31:00,167 --> 00:31:02,167
- Oh they're all
pretty much alike.

887
00:31:02,167 --> 00:31:04,067
This was just a little
easier, that's all.

888
00:31:04,067 --> 00:31:05,133
- Easier?

889
00:31:05,133 --> 00:31:06,633
Ha!

890
00:31:06,633 --> 00:31:08,233
Well, this just wants to get
away from me, that's all.

891
00:31:08,233 --> 00:31:09,467
- [Servo] Just drink.

892
00:31:09,467 --> 00:31:10,967
- Come on, let's get off
the flying kick, huh.

893
00:31:10,967 --> 00:31:12,867
We're gonna be on it every
day for the next six months.

894
00:31:12,867 --> 00:31:14,167
- Day and night.

895
00:31:14,167 --> 00:31:16,333
Hey, I live for this
stuff, don't you?

896
00:31:16,333 --> 00:31:18,700
- Sure, Bill, flying's
my first love right now.

897
00:31:18,700 --> 00:31:19,900
- [Mike] After drinking.

898
00:31:19,900 --> 00:31:21,367
- Suppose I weren't
a throttle jock,

899
00:31:21,367 --> 00:31:23,767
maybe I'd be on a navy
underwater demolition team

900
00:31:23,767 --> 00:31:26,233
or some other wild outfit, and
that would be my first love.

901
00:31:26,233 --> 00:31:27,767
- [Mike] Not decoupage?

902
00:31:27,767 --> 00:31:29,833
- You mean to say you didn't
want in this mans Air Force?

903
00:31:29,833 --> 00:31:30,667
- When I was in college.

904
00:31:30,667 --> 00:31:31,867
- [Mike] Drink.

905
00:31:31,867 --> 00:31:32,700
My dad wanted me
to get in the ROTC.

906
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:33,767
- [Servo] Oh boy.

907
00:31:33,767 --> 00:31:35,300
- [Mike] Liquor.

908
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:36,333
- My school just happened to
have an Air Force ROTC unit.

909
00:31:36,333 --> 00:31:37,533
- [Crow] Booze.

910
00:31:37,533 --> 00:31:38,467
- Then when I graduated,
he wanted me to get

911
00:31:38,467 --> 00:31:40,300
in the actual flying end of it,

912
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:41,133
so I'm here, and that's great.

913
00:31:41,133 --> 00:31:42,400
- [Servo] Gin.

914
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:43,667
- But I wasn't one of
these kids that used to

915
00:31:43,667 --> 00:31:44,900
hang around airports
just to be near pilots

916
00:31:44,900 --> 00:31:46,567
and planes and hangar talk.

917
00:31:46,567 --> 00:31:47,400
- [Mike] Okay, okay.

918
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:48,667
- Really love it.

919
00:31:48,667 --> 00:31:50,167
I wouldn't trade it
for anything, but.

920
00:31:50,167 --> 00:31:51,733
(burp)

921
00:31:51,733 --> 00:31:53,000
I don't see why we have to
breathe it day and night.

922
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:54,433
- Geez, I started a
friendly conversation,

923
00:31:54,433 --> 00:31:55,733
and he takes the floor.

924
00:31:55,733 --> 00:31:58,200
- Okay, sport, here's to
some really good flying.

925
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,400
- I'll drink to that.

926
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:02,467
- 17-and-a-half scotches later.

927
00:32:02,467 --> 00:32:05,900
- [Mike] (muffled) to realize
I had a aptitude for flying.

928
00:32:05,900 --> 00:32:07,833
'Course I'm as social
as the next guy,

929
00:32:07,833 --> 00:32:09,767
have I told you that, over?

930
00:32:11,167 --> 00:32:15,000
- [Servo] Playing tennis,
flying all with your new hair.

931
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:19,100
- Cordite four, join the
formation, we like you.

932
00:32:19,100 --> 00:32:21,233
- [Mike] The dentist
will see you shortly.

933
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:26,133
- Uh, anyone seen Francis Gary?

934
00:32:26,133 --> 00:32:28,100
Where'd he get off to, that nut?

935
00:32:28,100 --> 00:32:30,200
- [Mike] You know, we can
make fun of these guys,

936
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:32,433
but Saddam Hussein
ain't laughin' huh.

937
00:32:32,433 --> 00:32:33,367
(laughter)

938
00:32:33,367 --> 00:32:35,067
- [Servo] Mike, shall we?

939
00:32:35,067 --> 00:32:37,000
- [Mike] Oh, I'd
love to, thank you.

940
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:40,567
- (humming) The afternoon.

941
00:32:42,767 --> 00:32:44,333
- [Mike] You're as light as air.

942
00:32:44,333 --> 00:32:46,967
- [Servo] Oh, that's lovely,
where did you learn that step?

943
00:32:51,233 --> 00:32:52,533
- [Mike] Thank you.

944
00:32:52,533 --> 00:32:55,133
- [Servo] Oh, I am
tired, thank you.

945
00:32:55,133 --> 00:32:59,300
- Here, the Air Force escorts
in anew new to a golf game.

946
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:01,233
- [Mike] Yes, we've
traded quality education

947
00:33:01,233 --> 00:33:04,033
of a million kids
for these planes.

948
00:33:05,633 --> 00:33:07,367
- [Mike] Ah, lovely, lovely.

949
00:33:07,367 --> 00:33:09,233
- [Crow] Very nice.

950
00:33:09,233 --> 00:33:10,733
- [Servo] Ooh,
colonel, do laugh.

951
00:33:10,733 --> 00:33:12,767
- Well, gentlemen, now that
you've soloed in Starfighter,

952
00:33:12,767 --> 00:33:14,067
you're entitled to this patch.

953
00:33:14,067 --> 00:33:15,567
- [Mike] Oh great, a patch.

954
00:33:15,567 --> 00:33:16,833
- I'm sure you'll discover
that the next training phase

955
00:33:16,833 --> 00:33:19,200
is more exciting and
much more demanding.

956
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:20,667
Eventually, we'll be
depending on you to

957
00:33:20,667 --> 00:33:22,533
perform a variety of fine jobs.

958
00:33:22,533 --> 00:33:23,833
For instance, that
pilot right there,

959
00:33:23,833 --> 00:33:25,800
he's going up for
another high altitude

960
00:33:25,800 --> 00:33:27,267
side winder firing test.

961
00:33:27,267 --> 00:33:31,067
- Nope, just going to clean
out my plane. (chuckles)

962
00:33:31,067 --> 00:33:32,667
- Colonel Hunt, sir, they've
been looking for you.

963
00:33:32,667 --> 00:33:34,133
Telephone call from Washington.

964
00:33:34,133 --> 00:33:35,900
- And I've been looking
for you O'Brien.

965
00:33:35,900 --> 00:33:36,967
- [Mike] What's happening?

966
00:33:36,967 --> 00:33:38,433
- General has just been informed

967
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:39,700
that five technicians
from the Belgian Air Force

968
00:33:39,700 --> 00:33:41,400
will be on the base
sometime this evening,

969
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,300
and you are to
escort to escort them

970
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:44,533
during their stay here.

971
00:33:44,533 --> 00:33:46,367
- What, I'm setup for
night flying this week.

972
00:33:46,367 --> 00:33:47,633
(gulp)

973
00:33:47,633 --> 00:33:48,833
- I know, they'll
just have to wait

974
00:33:48,833 --> 00:33:49,833
until after they've seen
how we operate here.

975
00:33:49,833 --> 00:33:50,767
- Well, I'll be going up.

976
00:33:50,767 --> 00:33:52,067
- Ah-ah-ah, temper, temper.

977
00:33:52,067 --> 00:33:53,567
- Aw, nuts.

978
00:33:53,567 --> 00:33:57,067
(upbeat electronic music)

979
00:34:00,100 --> 00:34:01,033
- Colonel Hunt speaking.

980
00:34:01,033 --> 00:34:02,500
- Good morning, Colonel Hunt.

981
00:34:02,500 --> 00:34:04,167
You're a hard man to find.

982
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:05,000
- [Mike] Sarah?

983
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,167
- Who's this?

984
00:34:06,167 --> 00:34:07,400
- Well, it's a
little difficult to

985
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,267
introduce oneself
over the phone.

986
00:34:08,267 --> 00:34:09,767
- I sell Panola.

987
00:34:09,767 --> 00:34:11,500
- I'm John Witkowski, the
father of one of the pilots

988
00:34:11,500 --> 00:34:14,033
who transferred to your
command a couple of weeks ago.

989
00:34:14,033 --> 00:34:14,967
- Oh.

990
