00:49:35,200 --> 00:49:37,300
you'd tear it loose from
the plane in one burst.

1482
00:49:37,300 --> 00:49:38,467
- [Servo] Wow.

1483
00:49:38,467 --> 00:49:39,567
- Colonel Hunt
here had many kills

1484
00:49:39,567 --> 00:49:41,133
and as many probables
over France.

1485
00:49:41,133 --> 00:49:42,300
It's a standing joke around here

1486
00:49:42,300 --> 00:49:44,467
that he's not exactly
proficient with

1487
00:49:44,467 --> 00:49:45,933
anything that does
not shoot back.

1488
00:49:45,933 --> 00:49:47,233
- [Servo] So he's dumb.

1489
00:49:47,233 --> 00:49:48,467
- [Mike] Doesn't
translate well, but.

1490
00:49:49,867 --> 00:49:51,300
- From the Victorville
Chamber of Commerce meeting

1491
00:49:51,300 --> 00:49:53,333
where I gave 'em my
anti communist speech.

1492
00:49:53,333 --> 00:49:54,900
- [Mike] Again?

1493
00:49:54,900 --> 00:49:56,733
- I want you fellas to get
up there and do right by me

1494
00:49:56,733 --> 00:49:58,333
and knock the devil
out of that thing.

1495
00:49:58,333 --> 00:50:01,200
- [Mike] Well, he's crusty
but extremely unlikable.

1496
00:50:01,200 --> 00:50:02,133
- Mostly crusty.

1497
00:50:03,333 --> 00:50:05,300
Hey, they strapped the
general onto that one.

1498
00:50:06,733 --> 00:50:08,733
- [Servo] Ooh, at
least excuse yourself.

1499
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:16,067
- [Mike] Uh-oh, that
wasn't supposed to happen.

1500
00:50:16,067 --> 00:50:20,133
(suspenseful instrumental music)

1501
00:50:21,467 --> 00:50:23,067
- [Servo] Uh-huh.

1502
00:50:23,067 --> 00:50:24,800
- [Mike] Right.

1503
00:50:24,800 --> 00:50:27,167
- Wow, they've taken
Jarts to the next level.

1504
00:50:27,167 --> 00:50:29,400
(laughing)

1505
00:50:31,633 --> 00:50:33,200
- [Mike] Aw, the
plane is pregnant.

1506
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:35,533
(baby talk)

1507
00:50:40,900 --> 00:50:43,367
- [Servo] Geez, up or
down, you kids, up or down!

1508
00:50:47,333 --> 00:50:48,300
- [Mike] Ah yes.

1509
00:50:48,300 --> 00:50:50,167
- Ah, the association are back.

1510
00:50:50,167 --> 00:50:52,433
Is, are.

1511
00:50:52,433 --> 00:50:53,533
Was.

1512
00:50:53,533 --> 00:50:55,033
- [Servo] Whatever.

1513
00:50:55,033 --> 00:50:57,133
- [Mike] Steve, your head looks
like an egg from back here.

1514
00:50:57,133 --> 00:50:58,800
- [Servo] I suppose
their last project

1515
00:50:58,800 --> 00:51:00,767
before The Ray Conniff
Singers broke up.

1516
00:51:04,600 --> 00:51:06,000
This is high enough for me,

1517
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:07,333
thank you very much.

1518
00:51:10,200 --> 00:51:14,633
- [Mike] (humming) It's catchy.

1519
00:51:14,633 --> 00:51:15,567
- [Servo] Oh, Pueblo tapestry,

1520
00:51:15,567 --> 00:51:16,933
let's blow the hell out of it!

1521
00:51:18,933 --> 00:51:21,400
- This is still better
than Iron Eagle.

1522
00:51:21,400 --> 00:51:22,967
- [Servo] Cha-cha-cha.
(mimics static)

1523
00:51:22,967 --> 00:51:24,967
- [Voiceover] Cordite
lead, Cordite two.

1524
00:51:24,967 --> 00:51:26,800
- [Mike] Cordite two,
you're on the air.

1525
00:51:26,800 --> 00:51:28,100
What do you think of the
Clinton Administration?

1526
00:51:28,100 --> 00:51:29,300
- [Voiceover] Go ahead, two.

1527
00:51:29,300 --> 00:51:30,767
- [Voiceover] Lead,
I've got troubles here.

1528
00:51:30,767 --> 00:51:32,167
My number two hydraulic
system is dropping rapidly.

1529
00:51:32,167 --> 00:51:33,400
- [Servo] Hmm.

1530
00:51:33,400 --> 00:51:34,333
- [Voiceover] All right,
let's clear the range,

1531
00:51:34,333 --> 00:51:35,267
and I'll get on your wing.

1532
00:51:35,267 --> 00:51:36,600
Pick up a heading for the base.

1533
00:51:36,600 --> 00:51:38,500
- [Voiceover] Yes, sir.

1534
00:51:40,300 --> 00:51:42,533
- [Servo] Well, you can tell
it's a dangerous situation

1535
00:51:42,533 --> 00:51:44,400
by the music, tell 'em.

1536
00:51:44,400 --> 00:51:45,200
- Yes.

1537
00:51:47,467 --> 00:51:49,000
- [Voiceover] Cordite
two, any change yet?

1538
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:51,433
- [Voiceover] Negative, gauge
says there's nothing left.

1539
00:51:51,433 --> 00:51:52,533
- [Voiceover] Okay,
lower your airspeed

1540
00:51:52,533 --> 00:51:55,167
to 120 knots and drop your gear.

1541
00:51:56,333 --> 00:51:57,633
- Ah, it's a spare.

1542
00:51:57,633 --> 00:51:59,867
Good only for 10 miles
at 50 miles per hour.

1543
00:52:02,333 --> 00:52:05,000
- [Voiceover] Your gear looks
okay, are you indicating more?

1544
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:06,633
- [Voiceover] No sir, I've
got an unsafe gear indication,

1545
00:52:06,633 --> 00:52:09,833
and my number two hydraulic
system reads absolute zero.

1546
00:52:09,833 --> 00:52:11,333
- [Mike] What is right with you?

1547
00:52:11,333 --> 00:52:12,833
- [Voiceover] Just run your
manual emergency gear release.

1548
00:52:12,833 --> 00:52:15,267
- [Servo] Oh, and my tape
deck won't work either.

1549
00:52:19,267 --> 00:52:21,800
- [Voiceover] Cordite lead,
still reading unsafe here.

1550
00:52:21,800 --> 00:52:23,367
- [Servo] Hmm.

1551
00:52:23,367 --> 00:52:24,800
- [Voiceover] Hold, Cordite.

1552
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:26,000
Calling and requesting emergency
for straight in approach.

1553
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:28,400
- Uh, go ahead and
kiss your ass goodbye.

1554
00:52:28,400 --> 00:52:30,000
- [Voiceover] George
tower, Cordite lead.

1555
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:31,433
- [Mike] I'm incapable
of love, over.

1556
00:52:31,433 --> 00:52:32,800
- Cordite lead,
George tower over.

1557
00:52:32,800 --> 00:52:34,033
- [Voiceover]
George, Cordite lead.

1558
00:52:34,033 --> 00:52:35,633
Request emergency
landing for 104.

1559
00:52:35,633 --> 00:52:36,967
- [Mike] That's trash, oh.

1560
00:52:36,967 --> 00:52:38,300
- [Voiceover] Approximately
30 miles north.

1561
00:52:38,300 --> 00:52:39,800
Request straight in approach.

1562
00:52:39,800 --> 00:52:42,267
My wingman has a
hydraulic utility failure.

1563
00:52:42,267 --> 00:52:44,000
Landing gear down but
indicating unsafe.

1564
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:45,067
I'm declaring emergency.

1565
00:52:45,067 --> 00:52:46,567
- [Servo] And he's crying too.

1566
00:52:46,567 --> 00:52:48,133
- Roger, Cordite lead, we'll
clear the pattern for you

1567
00:52:48,133 --> 00:52:50,700
to land on runway one
six straight in approach.

1568
00:52:50,700 --> 00:52:51,867
- [Voiceover] Cordite check.

1569
00:52:53,267 --> 00:52:54,700
- Emergency, emergency.

1570
00:52:54,700 --> 00:52:56,267
F-104 hydraulic failure.

1571
00:52:56,267 --> 00:52:59,100
Landing from straight in
approach runway one six.

1572
00:52:59,100 --> 00:53:02,300
- Oh cheeks, we gotta
save baby pants.

1573
00:53:02,300 --> 00:53:03,867
(suspenseful music)

1574
00:53:03,867 --> 00:53:05,700
- [Servo] It sounds like
a Russian national anthem.

1575
00:53:05,700 --> 00:53:07,700
- [Mike] Yeah, they would.

1576
00:53:07,700 --> 00:53:10,733
- The turtle called Gabra
is approaching the base.

1577
00:53:10,733 --> 00:53:12,267
- [Servo] Whoa.

1578
00:53:12,267 --> 00:53:13,600
- [Mike] The hippies got those

1579
00:53:13,600 --> 00:53:14,800
when they were done with them.

1580
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:17,200
(laughs)

1581
00:53:17,200 --> 00:53:20,333
- A giant hippity hop
is called into action.

1582
00:53:21,700 --> 00:53:24,133
- Attention all aircraft,
vicinity George Air Force Base.

1583
00:53:24,133 --> 00:53:25,533
We have an emergency landing.

1584
00:53:25,533 --> 00:53:27,433
Be clear of George
traffic pattern.

1585
00:53:27,433 --> 00:53:28,967
I repeat, we have an emergency.

1586
00:53:28,967 --> 00:53:31,167
Maintain radio silence.

1587
00:53:31,167 --> 00:53:32,933
- [Servo] All this because
a girl wouldn't kiss him.

1588
00:53:32,933 --> 00:53:34,400
- [Voiceover] Cordite
two, any change yet?

1589
00:53:34,400 --> 00:53:36,100
- [Voiceover] Negative,
lead, same indications here.

1590
00:53:36,100 --> 00:53:38,500
- [Voiceover] Junior, prepare
that sweat that bird down.

1591
00:53:38,500 --> 00:53:40,133
- [Voiceover] I think
I can handle it, major.

1592
00:53:40,133 --> 00:53:42,500
I just hope this gear doesn't
fold up when I touch down.

1593
00:53:42,500 --> 00:53:43,467
- [Servo] Mm-hmm.

1594
00:53:43,467 --> 00:53:44,900
♪ We got a great big convoy, ♪

1595
00:53:44,900 --> 00:53:48,000
truckin' through the night.

1596
00:53:48,000 --> 00:53:50,800
- Oops, uh, sorry, it's just
my seatbelt's in the door.

1597
00:53:50,800 --> 00:53:52,267
- [Servo] Doh.

1598
00:53:52,267 --> 00:53:53,267
- [Voiceover] John, from here,
all three wheels are down

1599
00:53:53,267 --> 00:53:54,533
and appear to be locked tight.

1600
00:53:54,533 --> 00:53:56,033
- [Voiceover] Rog.

1601
00:53:56,033 --> 00:53:57,567
- [Mike] Hi Dwayne,
what's happening?

1602
00:53:57,567 --> 00:53:58,767
- [Voiceover] Stay
with you, I want you to

1603
00:53:58,767 --> 00:54:00,200
make a normal
approach in landing.

1604
00:54:00,200 --> 00:54:02,133
Emergency equipment
is standing by.

1605
00:54:02,133 --> 00:54:03,067
- [Servo] (mimics
static) Captain,

1606
00:54:03,067 --> 00:54:04,200
we're out of Colombia coffee.

1607
00:54:04,200 --> 00:54:07,600
(suspenseful music)

1608
00:54:07,600 --> 00:54:10,133
- I know I'm supposed to
feel something, but I don't.

1609
00:54:10,133 --> 00:54:12,267
- [Servo] Mm-mm, I'm with you.

1610
00:54:12,267 --> 00:54:13,333
- [Voiceover] George
tower, Cordite lead.

1611
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:15,467
We're five miles out on final.

1612
00:54:15,467 --> 00:54:17,000
- Cordite lead,
George tower, roger.

1613
00:54:17,000 --> 00:54:18,367
Traffic is clear
for you to land.

1614
00:54:18,367 --> 00:54:20,000
- [Servo] I'm going on break.

1615
00:54:20,900 --> 00:54:23,167
♪ Dum-dee-dum-dum. ♪

1616
00:54:23,167 --> 00:54:26,200
- This guy gets wigged out
if his floor mats are uneven.

1617
00:54:26,200 --> 00:54:29,433
(suspenseful music)

1618
00:54:29,433 --> 00:54:32,500
- [Servo] Did they ever consider
that this wasn't riveting?

1619
00:54:33,900 --> 00:54:35,800
- [Mike] Boy, the potential
for something to happen

1620
00:54:35,800 --> 00:54:38,533
is very high right now.

1621
00:54:38,533 --> 00:54:41,200
- You know, it's a, this is
about a lot more than flying.

1622
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:44,000
- [Mike] Yeah, yeah,
it's about landing too.

1623
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:47,200
- [Servo] Oh no not runway
two, we just seal coated it.

1624
00:54:47,200 --> 00:54:50,467
(suspenseful music)

1625
00:54:50,467 --> 00:54:55,300
- Whoo, I bet he feels a
little silly right now.

1626
00:54:55,300 --> 00:54:56,667
- [Mike] Well, that's
the moron's problem,

1627
00:54:56,667 --> 00:54:58,933
he's got parachutes
jammed in his plane.

1628
00:54:58,933 --> 00:54:59,867
- [Servo] Oh no wonder.

1629
00:54:59,867 --> 00:55:01,767
- Here come the three stooges.

1630
00:55:01,767 --> 00:55:04,633
(hums tune)

1631
00:55:04,633 --> 00:55:06,033
- [Voiceover] See,
John, no sweat.

1632
00:55:06,033 --> 00:55:07,900
Let the fire department
put the gear pins in,

1633
00:55:07,900 --> 00:55:09,267
and they'll throw the bird back.

1634
00:55:09,267 --> 00:55:11,133
- [Mike] Read some
of the gauges wrong.

1635
00:55:11,133 --> 00:55:13,400
It's different than
the other plane.

1636
00:55:13,400 --> 00:55:15,800
- This movie just faced us.

1637
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:19,200
- [Servo] Ah, one of the
great anticlimaxes, huh?

1638
00:55:19,200 --> 00:55:22,133
(triumphant music)

1639
00:55:24,533 --> 00:55:25,733
- [Mike] Uh, one more push.

1640
00:55:25,733 --> 00:55:28,133
We can see the head
now, you're doing fine.

1641
00:55:29,533 --> 00:55:30,967
- [Servo] John Glenn sings
the great love songs.

1642
00:55:30,967 --> 00:55:33,067
- Attention all aircraft,
vicinity George Air Force Base.

1643
00:55:33,067 --> 00:55:34,433
Emergency has terminated.

1644
00:55:34,433 --> 00:55:36,933
George open for normal traffic.

1645
00:55:36,933 --> 00:55:39,200
- [Mike] That was a great scene.

1646
00:55:39,200 --> 00:55:41,933
- Hey Stinky, you leave
now, you're out of the band!

1647
00:55:45,533 --> 00:55:47,867
- [Mike] That guys got a poster
of Mark Spitz in his locker.

1648
00:55:47,867 --> 00:55:49,067
- Who doesn't?

1649
00:55:49,067 --> 00:55:50,300
- You were the
one they're making

1650
00:55:50,300 --> 00:55:51,567
all of that fuss
about out there.

1651
00:55:51,567 --> 00:55:53,267
Hey, uh, you trying to
grab a satellite, boy?

1652
00:55:53,267 --> 00:55:55,400
- Mm-mm, it was a little
harry, but no sweat.

1653
00:55:55,400 --> 00:55:57,300
- Well, with all those
wagons out there,

1654
00:55:57,300 --> 00:55:59,467
somebody must have
worked up a little sweat.

1655
00:55:59,467 --> 00:56:00,833
- Well, sorry I
disappointed them.

1656
00:56:00,833 --> 00:56:02,333
- [Servo] Virginia Slim?

1657
00:56:02,333 --> 00:56:04,100
- Somebody's been trying to
get a hold of you all day.

1658
00:56:04,100 --> 00:56:05,300
Long distance.

1659
00:56:05,300 --> 00:56:07,433
You're supposed to
call, um, operator 12,

1660
00:56:07,433 --> 00:56:09,133
Washington, D.C.

1661
00:56:09,133 --> 00:56:10,633
- Right, thanks Gene.

1662
00:56:10,633 --> 00:56:12,500
- Hey, hey, do you have
any influence back there?

1663
00:56:12,500 --> 00:56:15,533
(mock laughter)

1664
00:56:15,533 --> 00:56:16,733
- Oh, nothing's wrong, Johnny.

1665
00:56:16,733 --> 00:56:18,333
We hadn't heard from
you for a while,

1666
00:56:18,333 --> 00:56:19,733
and we were wondering
if everything's all
right out there.

1667
00:56:19,733 --> 00:56:20,667
- [Servo] Yeah, is it?

1668
00:56:20,667 --> 00:56:22,100
- Oh Dad, everything's okay.

1669
00:56:22,100 --> 00:56:23,533
- [Mike] I just hate you.

1670
00:56:23,533 --> 00:56:24,800
- Hey, it's great to
hear from ya, how are ya?

1671
00:56:24,800 --> 00:56:26,367
- Feelin' tops, Johnny.

1672
00:56:26,367 --> 00:56:27,600
- [Mike] I miss Scott Thorson.

1673
00:56:27,600 --> 00:56:28,967
- But I was concerned about

1674
00:56:28,967 --> 00:56:30,567
not hearing from
you for so long.

1675
00:56:30,567 --> 00:56:33,100
- Oh I'm sorry, Dad, we've
been so busy here lately,

1676
00:56:33,100 --> 00:56:35,433
I guess I've been kind of lax
in writing to you and Mom.

1677
00:56:35,433 --> 00:56:36,267
- [Servo] Well, bye.

1678
00:56:36,267 --> 00:56:37,733
- How is she?

1679
00:56:37,733 --> 00:56:40,167
- Fine as usual, but you know
how she worries about you.

1680
00:56:40,167 --> 00:56:41,400
- [Mike] This guy's
Uncle Bead. (laughter)

1681
00:56:41,400 --> 00:56:43,467
- In all the time that
I was flying years ago,

1682
00:56:43,467 --> 00:56:45,567
I couldn't convince
her how safe it was.

1683
00:56:45,567 --> 00:56:47,133
- And now you're worried
about me, huh Dad?

1684
00:56:47,133 --> 00:56:48,600
- [Servo] Okay bye.

1685
00:56:48,600 --> 00:56:50,000
- Tell me, how's it going,
Johnny, any troubles?

1686
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:51,633
- Oh, nothing at
all to speak of.

1687
00:56:51,633 --> 00:56:53,433
We're going through the
typical transition training

1688
00:56:53,433 --> 00:56:55,167
that everybody
does in these 104s.

1689
00:56:55,167 --> 00:56:56,533
- Yes, I imagine you are.

1690
00:56:56,533 --> 00:56:58,000
- [Mike] Yes, I imagine so.

1691
00:56:58,000 --> 00:57:00,400
- Trouble is, is that, I've
been reading a number of reports

1692
00:57:00,400 --> 00:57:02,167
lately that come across my desk

1693
00:57:02,167 --> 00:57:04,467
telling me of all
sorts of accidents.

1694
00:57:04,467 --> 00:57:05,967
- Accidents, what kind?

1695
00:57:05,967 --> 00:57:06,967
- Put dad on the line.

1696
00:57:06,967 --> 00:57:09,033
- Usual kind.

1697
00:57:09,033 --> 00:57:11,533
Engine flame out,
things like that.

1698
00:57:11,533 --> 00:57:12,767
- [Servo] Drift of the page.

1699
00:57:12,767 --> 00:57:15,033
- In the fighters, the
pilot always bails out.

1700
00:57:15,033 --> 00:57:16,433
Not like in those
big jobs where you

1701
00:57:16,433 --> 00:57:19,100
keep flying if you
loose one engine.

1702
00:57:19,100 --> 00:57:21,067
- Oh, look Dad, I know
what you're driving at,

1703
00:57:21,067 --> 00:57:22,500
and the whole thing is silly.

1704
00:57:22,500 --> 00:57:24,367
There's been nothing
like that happening here,

1705
00:57:24,367 --> 00:57:26,733
and if it did, I'm sure I
could hack any emergency

1706
00:57:26,733 --> 00:57:29,400
where we go through these
recommended steps all the time.

1707
00:57:29,400 --> 00:57:32,000
- I still wish you'd
apply for a transfer,

1708
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:33,600
into a bigger outfit, you know.

1709
00:57:33,600 --> 00:57:36,100
- [Mike] Your father
and I are worried, son.

1710
00:57:37,500 --> 00:57:40,133
- Those B-58s will be coming
into their own shortly.

1711
00:57:40,133 --> 00:57:42,033
- But Dad, it just
isn't done that way.

1712
00:57:42,033 --> 00:57:44,167
You don't go hopping
around from place to place

1713
00:57:44,167 --> 00:57:46,133
because you want to try
out different methods.

1714
00:57:46,133 --> 00:57:47,333
- [Mike] Dad.

1715
00:57:47,333 --> 00:57:48,867
- Well, you should
know how they operate.

1716
00:57:48,867 --> 00:57:50,667
- I'm in a position to make
it real easy for you to get

